---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Community Guidelines"
  description="The shared agreements that make the Montessori Adolescent Collective a place worth being — how we talk to each other, what we share, and how concerns are handled."
  heroTitle="Community Guidelines"
  heroSubtitle="The agreements that keep this a place worth being."
>
  <div class="container guidelines">
    <p class="closing">
      Short version: protect the children in your care, be generous with what you
      know, and treat people the way you'd want a colleague to treat you on a
      hard day.
    </p>

    <p class="lede">
      The Collective is a small, private space for people doing real work with
      adolescents. It works because of how we treat each other, not because of
      rules. These guidelines exist so that expectations are clear, and so that
      when something goes wrong there is a fair way to handle it.
    </p>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Protect student privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This is the one we hold most firmly. When you talk about examples from
        your environment, do not share a student's personal information — no
        full name, school, family circumstances, or diagnosis. If you are
        describing a difficult situation, change identifying details.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Posting photos</h2>
      <p>
        If you share photos of your community as examples, those stay on this
        platform. They are not to be shared outside the Collective.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where young people are recognisable, make sure you have permission from
        their family for that specific use, and remember that anything posted
        here can be seen by every member.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>What is discussed in the Collective stays in the Collective</h2>
      <p>
        This is a safe place where practitioners can troubleshoot and help one
        another. Members share honestly about struggles in their schools and
        homes. Do not screenshot, forward, or repost what someone writes here
        without their permission.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Only give advice or guidance when it is asked for</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes people just want to share something they are proud of. Refrain
        from critiquing or offering feedback when it has not been explicitly
        asked for.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Uploading materials</h2>
      <p>
        Post your own materials freely. Do not upload training manuals, albums,
        purchased curricula, or copyrighted books that aren't yours to
        distribute — including AMI course materials. Linking to a source is
        always safe; uploading a copy often isn't.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Stay Montessori-based, or cite your source</h2>
      <p>
        Only share resources and posts that are Montessori based, or backed by
        science and research. If you share something from another school of
        education or thought, please cite the source.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stay true to Montessori philosophy — though modern neuroscience and
        research-backed principles and work are welcome here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>No selling</h2>
      <p>
        This is not a marketplace. Mentioning your own work when it genuinely
        answers someone's question is fine. Promotional posts, recruitment, and
        unsolicited pitches are not.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Not a substitute for professional help</h2>
      <p>
        Members are educators, not clinicians. If a young person is at risk of
        harm, contact the appropriate professionals and services where you are —
        not this forum.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>What isn't allowed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Harassment, personal attacks, or demeaning language about any person or group</li>
        <li>Content that identifies a child without their family's consent</li>
        <li>Sexual content, graphic violence, or material illegal where you or we are</li>
        <li>Impersonating another person or misrepresenting your credentials</li>
        <li>Spam, scraping, or bulk-messaging other members</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>How concerns are handled</h2>
      <p>
        If something is amiss, tell us — mention <strong>@jarinwadiwalla</strong>
        in a post, or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> directly. A person reads
        every one of these.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most issues are resolved with a quiet conversation. Where something needs
        more, we may remove the content, ask you to change it, or pause an
        account. Content that puts a child at risk, or that is illegal, is
        removed immediately and without warning.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your membership is paused and you think that's wrong, reply to any
        email from us and a person will look at it again.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Platform feedback</h2>
      <p>
        If you would like to see new functionality in the platform, tell Jarin —
        mention <strong>@jarinwadiwalla</strong> in a post, or
        <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. We have the flexibility to adapt this
        place to what we actually need.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want your account and posts deleted, ask us and we can do that
        as well.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Your information</h2>
      <p>
        Your profile shows the name and picture you choose. Your email address is
        never shown to other members. Files you upload are visible only to
        signed-in members, not to the public web or search engines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="guideline">
      <h2>Dues</h2>
      <p>
        Membership runs on dues, monthly or yearly, and they stay deliberately
        low. You can switch between the two, or cancel, at any time from
        Billing inside the Collective — you never need to email us to leave.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cancelling keeps your access until the period you've already paid for
        runs out. If a payment fails we pause your membership rather than
        closing it, and nothing you've posted is deleted; updating your card
        puts everything back.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="guidelines-cta">
      <a href="/collective/" class="btn-primary">About the Collective</a>
      <a href="/collective/portal/" class="btn-secondary">Go to the Collective</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Shown only to signed-in members who haven't accepted yet -->
    <section class="accept-box" id="accept-box" hidden>
      <h2>One thing before you come in</h2>
      <p>
        These guidelines are the whole rulebook. By continuing you're agreeing
        to hold to them.
      </p>
      <button id="accept-btn" type="button">I've read them — I accept</button>
      <p class="accept-error" id="accept-error" role="alert"></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  // The guidelines are public; the acceptance step only appears for a
  // signed-in member who hasn't accepted yet.
  (async () => {
    try {
      const me = await (await fetch('/api/community/me')).json();
      if (!me.signedIn || !me.needsGuidelines) return;
      const box = document.getElementById('accept-box')!;
      box.hidden = false;

      document.getElementById('accept-btn')!.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const btn = document.getElementById('accept-btn') as HTMLButtonElement;
        btn.disabled = true;
        const res = await fetch('/api/community/accept-guidelines', { method: 'POST' });
        if (res.ok) {
          window.location.href = me.needsProfile
            ? '/collective/portal/?welcome=1'
            : '/collective/start-here/';
        } else {
          btn.disabled = false;
          document.getElementById('accept-error')!.textContent =
            'That didn\'t save — please try again.';
        }
      });
    } catch {}
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .guidelines {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .guideline {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .guideline h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    color: var(--color-purple);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .guideline p {
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .guideline ul {
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .guideline li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .accept-box {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    background: var(--color-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .accept-box h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .accept-box button {
    background: var(--color-purple);
    color: var(--color-white);
    border: none;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .accept-box button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .accept-error {
    color: var(--color-terracotta-dark);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .closing {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--color-lavender);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    color: var(--color-purple);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .guidelines-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .btn-primary,
  .btn-secondary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--color-purple);
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-purple);
    color: var(--color-purple);
  }
</style>
